   "text": "This is a digoxigenin-type cardenolide with a four-sugar chain on the 3-OH. I read the stereochemistry from the drawing and then cross-checked it against the known digoxin SMILES, so it is partly from memory rather than fully derived from the wedges and hashes.\n\n- **Aglycone:** a steroid core with a butenolide (the unsaturated five-membered lactone) at C17, 12-OH, 14-OH, and methyls at C10 and C13. This is digoxigenin.\n- **Sugar chain at C3:** three 2,6-dideoxy-hexose (digitoxose) units joined in a row through their 4-O positions, each with a free 3-OH.\n- **Terminal sugar:** a glucose attached through O to C4 of the outermost digitoxose.\n\nTogether these match deslanoside, which is digoxin with a terminal glucose on the sugar chain. I took the digoxin stereodescriptors for the aglycone and the three digitoxoses. For the glucose I rewrote the standard \u03b2-D-glucopyranoside stereo so that it starts from the anomeric carbon.\n\nSMILES: C[C@H]1[C@@H]([C@H](C[C@@H](O1)O[C@@H]2[C@H](O[C@H](C[C@@H]2O)O[C@@H]3[C@H](O[C@H](C[C@@H]3O)O[C@H]4CC[C@]5([C@@H](C4)CC[C@@H]6[C@@H]5C[C@H]([C@]7([C@@]6(CC[C@@H]7C8=CC(=O)OC8)O)C)O)C)C)C)O)O[C@@H]9O[C@H](CO)[C@@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@H]9O"
  }
